Package: lazydesktop
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         git,
         shared-mime-info,
         libgl1,
         libxkbcommon-x11-0
Description: A native Git GUI for the KDE Plasma desktop
 LazyDesktop is a fast, native Git client built with Rust and GPUI.
 It integrates seamlessly with KDE Plasma and provides a clean interface
 for staging, committing, pushing, and managing Git repositories.
 .
 Features include:
  - Git status with per-file checkboxes and colored status indicators
  - Inline diff viewer with syntax highlighting
  - Commit with summary, description, skip-hooks, and co-authors
  - AI-powered commit message generation (OpenRouter, OpenAI, etc.)
  - Branch management (create, switch, delete)
  - Push / Fetch / Pull with smart cycling button
  - Commit history browser with file-level diff exploration
  - Custom YAML theme support

